Description: Causal inference as a Bayesian inverse problem via data
    assimilation. Implements the assimilative causal inference (ACI) metric,
    forward and backward causal influence ranges (CIR), closed-form
    conditional-Gaussian (CGNS) filtering/smoothing with a lagged-divergence
    table, ensemble Kalman-Bucy filter/smoother, and a
    collection of benchmark models. Based on Andreou, Chen & Bollt (2026)
    <doi:10.1038/s41467-026-68568-0>, Andreou & Chen (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2510.21889>, Jiang, Andreou, Reich & Chen (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2604.25157>, Moser, Chen & Andreou (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2605.22692>, and the adaptive online smoother of
    Andreou, Chen & Li (2026) <doi:10.1007/s00332-026-10271-x>.
